# Model & Tool Routing

AstraJax runs on a **think → build → grind** split. Match the model to the job, and
**flag when the current one looks wrong for the task.**

## The two pools (the fact that drives everything)

Cursor bills from two separate pools. Getting this wrong is the main way spend leaks.

| Pool | Models | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| **First-party** (subsidised, generous) | Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5, Composer 2.5, Auto | Cheap. Website and repo hands live here. |
| **Frontier / Other Models** (metered) | GPT Sol, Claude Opus 5, Sonnet 5, Kimi K3 | Scarce. Reserve for judgement. |

Matthew has repeatedly emptied the frontier pool while leaving first-party unused.
That is the failure mode this rule exists to prevent.

## The four tiers

| Tier | Job | Model | Pool |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Think** | Strategy, positioning, trade-offs, "should we?" | `gpt-5.6-sol-xhigh` | Frontier |
| **Challenge / taste** | Red-team, craft judgement, Doc Phase A triage | `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` (Sonnet 5 for structured verification) | Frontier |
| **Build** | Website vibecoding, scenic craft, multi-file product work | `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` | First-party |
| **Grind** | Automations, Trinity executors, repetitive mechanical edits | `composer-2.5-fast` | First-party |

These four tiers are **State A doctrine**. Live `.cursor/agents/` pins follow the operating pin state below.

Deliberate family split: OpenAI reasons, Anthropic challenges. Do not collapse both
sides onto one vendor — the point is independent judgement, not agreement.

## The hard rule

> **Frontier heads never perform mechanical edits.**
> If the job is files, edits, scaffolds, find-replace, or repeatable MCP writes,
> dispatch a first-party-pool subagent (Grok or Composer) via Task. Do not do it inline.

This single line is the leak. Everything else in this rule is bookkeeping.

## Kimi K3 — runtime-dependent, read carefully

K3's economics differ by runtime, so there is no single answer:

- **On HyperAgent:** K3 at low effort with high cache-hit rates is **cheap hands**.
  Ruth's executors are correctly pinned `moonshotai/kimi-k3` effort `low` there.
- **In Cursor:** K3 draws the **frontier** pool, so it competes with Sol and Opus 5.
  Treat it as **escalation only**, when Grok has failed the same task twice.

Do not pin K3 in Cursor agent frontmatter. Cursor twins of HyperAgent agents should
mirror the **doctrine**, not the slug.

